{"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","file":"scripts/grokbot-headless-dispatch.mjs","line":176,"problem":"Nothing in the dispatcher checks that the public client actually has the hash the ticket names. workerPrompt only checks the format, `/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/u.test(job.clientSha256)`, and tells the agent to download https://grokbot-mcp.24histories.com/grokbot-mcp-client.mjs and compare it with ${job.clientSha256}. prepareWake checks app readiness and capacity but never fetches the public client to compare its SHA-256. The server also serves that file with `cache-control: public, max-age=300`.","trigger":"The host issues a sealed-review ticket with the new client hash shortly after deploying, while a cache within the 300-second window still serves the old client. Alternatively, the host computes clientSha256 from a working-tree file that differs from the deployed one.","consequence":"The run fails closed. The agent sees the hash mismatch and stops before doing any work, as instructed, and nothing is sent with an unverified client. But the job was already reserved as 'dispatching' and the model was woken without doing any work, so the host must write an attempt:2 retry ticket. Because dispatchJobKey does not include clientSha256, a corrected hash cannot be redispatched any other way.","requiredFix":"In prepareWake, before the 'dispatching' reservation, fetch the public client URL unauthenticated (no bearer), compute its SHA-256 and refuse to wake unless it equals job.clientSha256. Consider sending `cache-control: no-store` for the client file, or a versioned URL. Add a test showing a mismatch leaves no reservation and no wake."},{"severity":"low","file":"scripts/grokbot-mcp-client.mjs","line":152,"problem":"The version guard requires exact equality, `initialized?.result?.serverInfo?.version !== '1.1.0'`, rather than a minimum version or a review-capability marker.","trigger":"Any later server version bump, for example to 1.1.1 or 1.2.0 for an unrelated fix, while remote machines still run this client.","consequence":"Every review resume or submit fails with 'requires the reviewed MCP server version1.1.0' until every remote client is updated again. This fails closed and loses no work, but it couples unrelated server releases to a client rollout.","requiredFix":"Accept versions at or above 1.1.0, or check an explicit capability the server advertises in serverInfo or instructions. Keep refusing servers below 1.1.0, as the new regression test checks."}]}
